1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,439
or Windows to look for these edges.

2
00:00:03,439 --> 00:00:06,400
And then the second hidden layer is
looking at bigger window

3
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:10,200
and the third hidden layer is looking at
even bigger window.

4
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:13,439
So these little neurons visualizations

5
00:00:13,439 --> 00:00:17,280
actually correspond to different size
regions in the image.

6
00:00:17,280 --> 00:00:20,600
Just for fun, let's see what happens if
you were to train

7
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:23,800
this neural network on a different data
set,

8
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:28,800
say on lots of pictures of cars, a picture
on the side.

9
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:34,200
The same learning algorithm if it's us to
detect cars

10
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:37,520
will then learn edges in the first layer.

11
00:00:37,520 --> 00:00:39,359
So pretty similar.

12
00:00:39,359 --> 00:00:41,920
But then they'll learn to detect parts of
cars

13
00:00:41,920 --> 00:00:45,679
in the second hidden layer and then more
complete car shapes

14
00:00:45,679 --> 00:00:47,480
in the third hidden layer.

15
00:00:47,480 --> 00:00:52,120
So just by feeding it different data,

16
00:00:52,120 --> 00:00:54,000
the neural network automatically learns

17
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:56,400
to detect very different features,

18
00:00:56,399 --> 00:01:01,839
so as to try to make predictions of car
detection

19
00:01:01,839 --> 00:01:04,000
or person recognition or whatever

20
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:07,000
is a particular given task that is trained
on.

